# Next step events matrix (worksheet)

Use this page to decide which events appear in ExUI **Next steps** for each role and case state.
When the **Desired** columns are filled in, they can be applied in the case-type
`*Configuration` classes (`.forStates` / `.forStateTransition` + `.grant`).

Related: [State and event model](/state-event-model.html), [CCD architecture — States and events](/ccd-architecture.html#states-and-events).

## How to fill this in

1. For each case type, complete the **Desired** columns (event ids, comma-separated, or `—` for none).
2. Leave system-only / `NEVER_SHOW` events out of Next steps unless you intentionally want them visible.
3. Field `showCondition`s (e.g. TE9 only when `applicationForm="TE9"`) still apply on top of state/role rules — note those in the event catalogue if you change them.
4. Create journeys (`uploadBatch`, and system create events) are **not** case-scoped Next steps; they are listed separately.

Legend for **Current** columns: what the POC grants today for Next-step visibility
(role has C/U on the event, and the event is not `NEVER_SHOW`).

## Roles

| Label | Java (`UserRole`) | IDAM role | Typical Next-step use |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| System | `SYSTEM` | `caseworker-tec-system` | Integrations / scripts — usually `NEVER_SHOW`, not in Next steps |
| Clerk / caseworker | `CLERK` | `caseworker-tec` | Primary Next-step actor on TEC / TEC_EXCEPTION |
| Local authority | `LOCAL_AUTHORITY` | `caseworker-tec-la` | Limited; CaseAccessCategories on TEC / TEC_BATCH; shuttered on TEC_EXCEPTION |

